course: dictionary
lesson: 11625
title: Apt: just right, or likely to
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Apt is an adjective with three meanings you will meet. It can mean suitable or just right, it can mean likely to do something, and in old books it can mean quick to learn. Read the words around it to find which meaning fits. «Her title was an apt choice for a story about a brave little fox.» Here apt means suitable, just right for that story.
explain: «Sam is apt to forget his PE kit on Mondays.» When apt is followed by to and a verb, it means he often tends to do that thing. Check it by swapping in the meaning: "Sam often tends to forget his kit" still makes sense, so you have the right meaning.
explain: «The old book called Tom an apt pupil, because he learned his times tables in a week.» Calling a pupil apt is old-fashioned, and the clue is learned so quickly. When apt describes a learner, think quick to learn.
fact: Apt means suitable or just right for the situation.
fact: «An apt description» is a description that fits the thing exactly.
fact: Apt to do something means you often tend to do it, as in «He is apt to forget».
fact: In old-fashioned writing, «an apt pupil» is a pupil who learns quickly.
fact: Check the words after apt: if to and a verb follow, it means likely to.
exercise: «Her song was an apt choice for the sad, rainy day.» What does apt mean here? | *Suitable and just right | Lost | Old and dusty | Very loud
exercise: «Ben is apt to lose his pencil case.» What does apt to mean? | *He often tends to lose it | He found it again | He is never going to lose it | He is a very fast runner
exercise: «The teacher called Amira an apt pupil.» In this old-fashioned use, what does apt mean? | *Quick to learn | Lazy and slow | Tall for her age | Rude and bossy
test: «Please give an apt answer to the question.» What does apt mean? | Loud and bossy | *Suitable, just right for the question | Gone for good
test: «Mum is apt to sing in the bath.» What does this mean? | *She often tends to sing in the bath | She sings only on Sundays | She hates singing | She is singing right now and will never stop
exam: «The picture was an apt match for the poem, and Ella is apt to notice small details.» What does apt mean in the second part? | Quick learner | *Likely to, tends to | Rude | Suitable
